<title>USA: Physio-Control lower 1997 revs.</title>
<headline>Physio-Control lower 1997 revs.</headline>
<dateline>REDMOND, Wash. 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Physio-Control Holding Corp, which Wednesday reported higher revenues in the second quarter and six month period, warned full year sales could be as much as five percent below 1996 levels.</p>
<p>In a statement, President and Chief Operating Officer Robert Guezurago cited uncertainty in international markets, continued soft demand in the hospital sector market and purchasing deferrals in anticipation of 1998 product introductions.</p>
<p>Last year, the company had revenues of $48.8 million.</p>
<p>Physio-Control makes an integrated line of non-invasive emergency cardiac defibrillator/pacemaker and vital sign assessment and related devices.</p>
</text>
